{:edb/db-before-t 2557 :edb/db-after-t 2558 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535870 50 #inst "2026-10-09T09:27:10.240Z" 13194139535870 true] [17592186078347 1020 #edb/ref 17592186371487 13194139535870 true] [17592186078348 1020 #edb/ref 17592186371491 13194139535870 true] [17592186078349 1020 #edb/ref 17592186371495 13194139535870 true] [17592186078349 1020 #edb/ref 17592186371498 13194139535870 true] [17592186371487 1017 #edb/ref 17592186371488 13194139535870 true] [17592186371487 1089 "q-346043" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371487 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535870 true] [17592186371487 1100 "Given that ${\\int }_{6}^{0}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=4,$ calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{6}(5f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{6}(5f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371487 1113 #uuid "8f9f00b1-7b9d-5c2d-924d-2b87fbdf35be" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371487 1145 "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{6}^{0}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}(5f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5(-4)\\,+\\,x\\,{|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =-20\\,+\\,(6-0) \\\\  & =-20\\,+\\,6 \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371488 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371489 13194139535870 true] [17592186371488 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371490 13194139535870 true] [17592186371488 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535870 true] [17592186371488 1041 "field-1" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371488 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371490 13194139535870 true] [17592186371488 1110 #uuid "f25acaa6-6b20-51a5-8263-75f78e25820b" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371489 1034 "26" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371489 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535870 true] [17592186371489 1111 #uuid "703ed312-09c5-5253-91b6-f0d434be889d" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371490 1034 "-14" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371490 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535870 true] [17592186371490 1111 #uuid "1fa56dd7-6869-5784-aa0a-edc637661c42" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371491 1017 #edb/ref 17592186371492 13194139535870 true] [17592186371491 1089 "q-346195" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371491 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535870 true] [17592186371491 1100 "Given that ${\\int }_{3}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0$ and ${\\int }_{7}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5,$ then what is ${\\int }_{3}^{10}(3f(x)-4)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{3}^{10}(3f(x)-4)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371491 1113 #uuid "9f83467c-530c-58f9-8cd1-4868e8f44e12" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371491 1145 "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{7}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\\,{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n0+5\\,=\\,{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{10}(3f(x)-4)\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,4{\\int }_{3}^{10}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(5)\\,-\\,4\\cdot x{|}_{3}^{10} \\\\  & =15\\,-\\,4(10-3) \\\\  & =15-28 \\\\  & =-13\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371492 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371493 13194139535870 true] [17592186371492 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371494 13194139535870 true] [17592186371492 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535870 true] [17592186371492 1041 "field-1" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371492 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371494 13194139535870 true] [17592186371492 1110 #uuid "96e52d5e-ec5b-5638-bfa7-eefc112d12f2" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371493 1034 "11" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371493 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535870 true] [17592186371493 1111 #uuid "78fd6ee6-5862-5ba8-a58d-cb3096d027a1" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371494 1034 "-13" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371494 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535870 true] [17592186371494 1111 #uuid "e9c742a4-d2a2-5ce3-ba0a-4aecf4d8b2db" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371495 1017 #edb/ref 17592186371496 13194139535870 true] [17592186371495 1089 "q-346219" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371495 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535870 true] [17592186371495 1100 "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that ${\\int }_{5}^{-1}7\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=14$ and ${\\int }_{-4}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{-4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371495 1113 #uuid "cf40ca30-e264-5872-9e23-27d42025a110" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371495 1145 "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{-1}7\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =14 \\\\ 7{\\int }_{5}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =14 \\\\ -7{\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =14 \\\\ {\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371496 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371497 13194139535870 true] [17592186371496 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535870 true] [17592186371496 1041 "field-1" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371496 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371497 13194139535870 true] [17592186371496 1110 #uuid "4bc84e42-6427-5f88-b8fb-ad51dd36c9c9" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371497 1034 "-\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371497 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535870 true] [17592186371497 1111 #uuid "010f6d81-ea51-5c35-afe3-92e501cf4cba" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371498 1017 #edb/ref 17592186371499 13194139535870 true] [17592186371498 1089 "q-4797" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371498 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535870 true] [17592186371498 1100 "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a  function such that ${\\int }_{2}^{-2}\\frac{1}{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3$ and ${\\int }_{2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=10.$  What is the value of ${\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371498 1113 #uuid "e557d0aa-f53c-521a-8a1c-fd93dd8bf83a" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371498 1145 "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{-2}\\frac{1}{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3 \\\\ {\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12+10 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371499 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371500 13194139535870 true] [17592186371499 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371501 13194139535870 true] [17592186371499 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371502 13194139535870 true] [17592186371499 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371503 13194139535870 true] [17592186371499 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371504 13194139535870 true] [17592186371499 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535870 true] [17592186371499 1041 "selection" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371499 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371501 13194139535870 true] [17592186371499 1110 #uuid "d41272b3-dba2-5744-a3aa-ead96b62928c" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371500 1034 "20" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371500 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535870 true] [17592186371500 1111 #uuid "9af75731-9d6b-570c-9e38-da632e4e2cbd" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371501 1034 "22" 13194139535870 true] [17592186371501 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535870 true] [17592186371501 1111 #uuid "2f527ab2-4d47-509b-afc6-2fde0d5098ba" 131941